keys changed"] [583 4 "// when it meets an item it did not expect (dictiter_iternextkey_lock_held, dictreviter_iter_lock_held;"] [584 4 "// queue 203: test_reversed_dict_after_clear_and_restore; before it any change of the keys was one)"] [589 4 "// compacted since (CPython's resize, at other moments): the positions lost, the keys changed"] [621 3 "// __reduce__ is dictiter_reduce: (iter, (list,)), the list the items a copy of the iterator would give,"] [622 3 "// the iterator itself not advanced (queue 211: test_dict's six *iterator_pickling tests)"] [665 2 "// a view's mapping: a mappingproxy of its dict (dictview_mapping; queue 203: test_views_mapping)"] [697 1 "// dictViewCompare is dictview_richcompare: the sizes, then every item of one in the other by the other's"] [698 1 "// containment (an items view's: the key looked up, the values compared), no set made (queue 203: an unhashable"] [699 1 "// value compared, test_errors_in_view_containment_check)."] [781 1 "// dictMissing is d[k] on a dict subclass with __missing__: the method called with the key."] [797 1 "// newDictSubclass makes an instance of a dict subclass; PY5c sets it (by default the base value: PY5c wraps it)."] [834 3 "// the key hashed and looked up once (dict_setdefault_ref; queue 203: test_setdefault_atomic)"] [880 5 "// the slot leaves the index too: a later key of its hash looked up entries[i] past the end"] [881 5 "// (PY6e's REQUEST: test_os's mapping tests popitem then set)"] [882 5 "// the popped entry and the holes after it leave the index too: a later key appended at their"] [883 5 "// positions is found by its own chain only"] [920 2 "// dict.fromkeys, a class method (dict_fromkeys: cls() filled by its __setitem__; PY7: it was a plain built-in,"] [921 2 "// bound to an instance, d.fromkeys(keys) iterated d)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[96 28] [120 25] [140 17] [140 47] [147 35] [162 22] [163 25] [175 24] [296 31] [309 12] [309 32] [320 55] [340 23] [344 13] [344 